{"id": "EUVD-2026-82244", "enisaUuid": "a421f39d-0975-3b7b-996a-8f58ec0171ef", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbus: mhi: ep: Fix device refcount leak in the error path of MHI device creation\n\nmhi_ep_create_device() takes one device reference for the UL channel and\nanother for the DL channel after allocating the transfer device. These\nreferences are normally released by mhi_ep_destroy_device() before the\ndevice itself is removed.\n\nIf dev_set_name() or device_add() fails, the error path currently drops\nonly one reference. The remaining channel references keep the device\nfrom being released and leave the channels associated with a device that\nwas never registered.\n\nRoute both failures through a common unwind path that drops the DL\nchannel reference, the UL channel reference, and the initial reference\nfrom device_initialize().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8acc3813ab5015af73eeb74c9032443162f122d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51ddb831a36102fd0ea25f354935e49abce9f0a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fae8fd4adc7f4765463ddeb1a5fad23936432f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5587e7871ce994bb079f97fe7e430d99627e5292", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f3f64faee335eb678fd7dca7b95dfe3d0b271fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f12862600bb70e599a614d706a095ea5f8f9858"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93136", "GHSA-4w2p-3v8x-m8hh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bfb1d03-5542-3399-95a9-75e2ab06ce5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}, {"id": "0f4983d7-b7e7-3937-bb99-79caf37e2028", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "1beaa533-b1bd-39b1-b078-cece25cab392", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297c77a0f27312b9a04696018c4cbd47926ca92b <5587e7871ce994bb079f97fe7e430d99627e5292"}, {"id": "3b5ba455-3607-3d3d-ab6e-f6e1ddfe6397", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "67355f9c-dd27-3f46-95c9-56f05b333a88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8b687483-7970-380d-aa86-07a061c9967e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "adf157c2-98a7-3247-aa3d-808688b24ebc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "c1e98f53-e746-3588-90e1-a82d5b3848d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297c77a0f27312b9a04696018c4cbd47926ca92b <51ddb831a36102fd0ea25f354935e49abce9f0a1"}, {"id": "c5f8d4f5-86ad-3934-a5f2-491748b3121b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297c77a0f27312b9a04696018c4cbd47926ca92b <8f3f64faee335eb678fd7dca7b95dfe3d0b271fd"}, {"id": "c6033f85-3982-3a48-bd57-188d03cdc555", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297c77a0f27312b9a04696018c4cbd47926ca92b <8acc3813ab5015af73eeb74c9032443162f122d1"}, {"id": "cbeba486-611c-37d6-b1e1-e55eab7df187", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297c77a0f27312b9a04696018c4cbd47926ca92b <6f12862600bb70e599a614d706a095ea5f8f9858"}, {"id": "d175aa81-3981-33d4-9a32-34872e22da14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "f8a12c8f-94f5-32ab-ba19-9ad9a8ccb158", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297c77a0f27312b9a04696018c4cbd47926ca92b <4fae8fd4adc7f4765463ddeb1a5fad23936432f6"}, {"id": "f96ee53d-3c04-3229-830e-5285929430ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}], "enisaIdVendor